{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1421049-character-advancement","id":1421049,"title":"Character Advancement","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-10-30T13:45:55-07:00","id":1421049,"title":"Character Advancement","content":"So, I'm running a game where the characters start at Origin-level and the game gradually amps up until they are Hero-level. So I have a few questions:<br /> <br /> How do you increase the number of calling dots? (Is it that every time you buy a knack in the calling, you get a new calling dot?)<br /> How do you adopt new callings? (I assume it's the way you would change callings but without the failure deed needed)<br /> <br /> And two &quot;opinion&quot; questions<br /> Do you think characters should be &quot;upgraded&quot; one at a time, over several sessions, or figure out a way that, offscreen, they are all visited around the same time and manage to get empowered?<br /> How do you manage cultural appropriation in your game? Just stick to mythologies you are very familiar with? Stick a big disclaimer in front of the game? Talk to the players? (Currently doing all three)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25668,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25668-geomancer","user":"Geomancer","date":". 10-30-2020, 04:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25668-geomancer","name":"Geomancer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-30T14:59:16-07:00","id":1421055,"title":"","content":"1. You gain a Calling Dot every even Legend rank. So +1 at Legend 2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12. This probably means most of your players will have more Knacks then they have Knack Slots.<br /> 2. You have to perform a Failure Deed to 'weaken' a Calling at Hero Tier, and then you can perform an Adoption Deed to replace one Calling with another. There's a stage in Demigod Play where you can swap a Calling for another each session.<br /> <br /> As for the others... I'd have the Visitations occur within the same approximate time frame, through a bunch of side scenes. Having players get too uneven in power level gives me hives.<br /> <br /> As for managing cultural appropriation... Research and try to do right, but it's absolutely okay to say upfront &quot;I do not know enough to touch this so we're going to focus on something else&quot; with your players. My general advice is try to do some research and keep aware of potential pitfalls, and if you find out or realize you did something Not Cool then for the love of your Gods of choice <i>do not double down</i>. It's okay to make mistakes as long as you learn from them and try to be better. Keeping in communication with your players is a smart choice, keep at that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-30T15:09:51-07:00","id":1421057,"title":"","content":"You get a new Calling dot whenever you reach an even-numbered Legend point up to Legend ten, so you get one at 2,4, 6, 8, and ten. The exception being Legend one which gives you four dots. You first adopt new Callings at your Visitation. By upgraded I assume you mean the Visitation? Normally in my experience it\u2019s a mix of both, all the Visitations happen around the same time narratively but they are usually roleplayed out one at a time in one on one sessions. And for the second question, the best thing to do is try to be respectful of the culture in questions, don\u2019t fall into stereotypes such as \u201cnoble savage\u201d and such, and of course do your research whenever possible","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-30T16:18:36-07:00","id":1421062,"title":"","content":"As someone that feels rather strongly about cultural appropriation?<br /> <br /> If it's a private game with just you and your friends? Do your best, but have fun. You're not likely to hurt someone with inappropriate uses of cultural material in a small game that will likely never be talked about by more than a dozen people.<br /> <br /> Scion tries to be as respectful as it can, but it's not an academic source on comparative religion. It's fine to approach it as a game and not worry about getting every last little detail right. People can always delve deeper into things if the game inspires them too. Just try to watch out for anyone that starts thinking they've learned everything these is to learn from a game, instead of seeing it as a starting point.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-30T17:00:23-07:00","id":1421068,"title":"","content":"Great, thanks for helping me understand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25668-geomancer","name":"Geomancer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}